{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant","id":1417071,"title":"DCU/MU Character builds for Aberrant?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-10-06T15:41:14-07:00","id":1417071,"title":"DCU/MU Character builds for Aberrant?","content":"While I personally feel the Aberrant world is a interesting blend of Iron &amp; Modern age comics in print, I have a number of friends who are die hard fans of the DC and Marvel comics franchises. Unfortunately, since the rules are available to backers only and I didn't get in on time for that, I was wondering if there are any backers who made examples or threads of anyone putting iconic characters of those studios in Aberrant terms? I.E. Batman, Magneto, Green Lantern, Captain America, etc.<br /> <br /> TIA","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-06T18:37:39-07:00","id":1417089,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m not familiar with any but that\u2019s a good idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T18:10:04-07:00","id":1417229,"title":"","content":"I was going to but there was much confusion with how some of the aberrant powers worked when the kickstarter came out and so I decided to just wait before diving into the deep end of character building. I think a lot of others did the same. Though if you look around the forum with Aberrant you might find some basic ideas posted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T18:55:30-07:00","id":1417234,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar661_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"661\" data-vbnamecard=\"661\">LordHeru</a> has a good point. Maybe best to wait till after the final product comes out on DTRPG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-07T19:26:13-07:00","id":1417236,"title":"","content":"There were two threads that I know of that discussed stats for the Hulk. I posted my version in the second thread:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk\"> Is there a way to create Hulk? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I mean, I considered simply tying dormancy to multiple personality disorder, but that really isn't good enough. Is there a way to have stats shift from mega strength and stamina in one personality, to mega intelligence in the other? </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition\"> CHALLENGE! Build the Hulk in Aberrant 1st Edition &amp; 2nd (Beta) Edition!!! - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I am curious how the two additions differ in bringing PC concepts to life. I would like to see how others can use Marvel's Incredible Hulk as a base 'concept' to show the PC creation system's in action. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A few big problems with making comic book character conversions at this time is that the Power Suite rules (which make your powers much more versatile) were getting an overhaul post-kickstarter, I'm pretty sure the Durability mega-edge was getting reworked, and the Transformation power (which I used to model the Hulk) seemed simultaneously too powerful and too restrictive.<br /> <br /> Going further into creating the Hulk, Transformation assumes everyone gets an infinite number of alternate forms even at level 1. There doesn't seem to be any default way to lower stats (like the Hulk being less intelligent than Dr. Banner). You can use it for physical Mega-Attributes, but not the associated Mega-Edges. So making the Hulk using the kickstarter presentation of the Transformation power requires a lot of Storyteller decisions, which is odd since a regular guy who transforms into a big, tough tank is a simple and frequently used trope.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T04:58:57-07:00","id":1417304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1417236#post1417236\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were two threads that I know of that discussed stats for the Hulk. I posted my version in the second thread:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk\"> Is there a way to create Hulk? - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1342535-is-there-a-way-to-create-hulk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I mean, I considered simply tying dormancy to multiple personality disorder, but that really isn't good enough. Is there a way to have stats shift from mega strength and stamina in one personality, to mega intelligence in the other? </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition\"> CHALLENGE! Build the Hulk in Aberrant 1st Edition &amp; 2nd (Beta) Edition!!! - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1356470-challenge-build-the-hulk-in-aberrant-1st-edition-2nd-beta-edition </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> I am curious how the two additions differ in bringing PC concepts to life. I would like to see how others can use Marvel's Incredible Hulk as a base 'concept' to show the PC creation system's in action. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A few big problems with making comic book character conversions at this time is that the Power Suite rules (which make your powers much more versatile) were getting an overhaul post-kickstarter, I'm pretty sure the Durability mega-edge was getting reworked, and the Transformation power (which I used to model the Hulk) seemed simultaneously too powerful and too restrictive.<br /> <br /> Going further into creating the Hulk, Transformation assumes everyone gets an infinite number of alternate forms even at level 1. There doesn't seem to be any default way to lower stats (like the Hulk being less intelligent than Dr. Banner). You can use it for physical Mega-Attributes, but not the associated Mega-Edges. So making the Hulk using the kickstarter presentation of the Transformation power requires a lot of Storyteller decisions, which is odd since a regular guy who transforms into a big, tough tank is a simple and frequently used trope.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. I didn\u2019t read the Kickstarter so I wasn\u2019t familiar with all those issues. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-08T06:34:29-07:00","id":1417318,"title":"","content":"This issues are not that big, but they do limit how to model characters.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Durability (and in fact all armor like powers) were described using a terms that don\u2019t fit the rules and were not explained anywhere, but could be understood.<br /> <br /> Transformation is the Beast Bot power, transform into animals or gain powers related to physical body, and fir that ends it works fine, there is also material chameleon, that is similar but copying material properties, also works fine (except for interacting with some powers) but there is no \u201celemental body\u201d or \u201calternate form\u201d or anything similar that transform you into a single alternate form, like the Hulk, Colossus, Human Torch etc, characters that have a set of powers in their human form and have another form with another set of powers (big, green and mega strong) or a more powerful set of powers (Biler proof, can fly, etc).<br /> <br /> The technique issue is the least of the problems as Danielle already told how it\u2019s going to work, but the point is, the way it was written in the manuscript creates some loop holes that make you capable of infinite powers of same level as long as you have 1 tag added to the power. Danielle suggested it would become a Mega Edge that allow you get one additional power (technique) to your power array per dot in the Mega Edge, it creates a limit of 1 + quantum powers per power suit (as intended before).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-14T13:55:50-07:00","id":1418243,"title":"","content":"My apologies all, life, work, computer going super-critical, prevented me from replying till now. Thank you to those who responded already:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1417318#post1417318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This issues are not that big, but they do limit how to model characters.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe Durability (and in fact all armor like powers) were described using a terms that don\u2019t fit the rules and were not explained anywhere, but could be understood.<br /> <br /> Transformation is the Beast Bot power, transform into animals or gain powers related to physical body, and fir that ends it works fine, there is also material chameleon, that is similar but copying material properties, also works fine (except for interacting with some powers) but there is no \u201celemental body\u201d or \u201calternate form\u201d or anything similar that transform you into a single alternate form, like the Hulk, Colossus, Human Torch etc, characters that have a set of powers in their human form and have another form with another set of powers (big, green and mega strong) or a more powerful set of powers (Biler proof, can fly, etc).<br /> <br /> The technique issue is the least of the problems as Danielle already told how it\u2019s going to work, but the point is, the way it was written in the manuscript creates some loop holes that make you capable of infinite powers of same level as long as you have 1 tag added to the power. Danielle suggested it would become a Mega Edge that allow you get one additional power (technique) to your power array per dot in the Mega Edge, it creates a limit of 1 + quantum powers per power suit (as intended before).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, interesting in a semi-negative sort of way. My group are all MM-2e/3e vets and are very creative using that ruleset for all manner of power levels, but as with most d20 systems, step outside of the combat arena and things drop off in satisfaction. We were very pleased with Scion 2e, and the thought was to recreate our library of MU/DCU stated out for MM3e into Aberrant. Both as a learning exercise and to create a usable library of npcs. We looked at the old Aberrant rules, but given how different Scion 1E vs 2E was, we figured it was best to come at it fresh so to absorb the ruleset without any bad habits ingrained from the previous version (we had a bit of a time adjusting from Scion's 1E to 2E, so trying to learn our lesson as it were).<br /> <br /> Several of my group like the alternate form idea with trade offs, such as Etrigan the Demon (DCU), or Legion (MU) to name a few, basically themes where the character is based on alternate forms or other similar designs. One of the go-to starter exercises usually consists of constructing Batman, Green Lantern, Wolverine and Spiderman (all with a couple of variants based on published storylines), and comparing it to other fan versions posted on boards.<br /> <br /> But since it seems there are some significant revisions happening before release, guess we'll have to wait for it's release and give it a bit of time for a errata release (there's always one in my experience) to iron out the kinks.<br /> <br /> If anyone has any further input or ideas of good practices, I'm very receptive and grateful for any suggestions.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-15T18:46:23-07:00","id":1418459,"title":"","content":"Batman, Spider-Man, and Wolverine shouldn't be too hard to build using the kickstarter preview manuscript, but Green Lantern is likely to be difficult no matter how polished things get, since the guy can literally do almost anything.<br /> <br /> For Batman, just building a highly competent human character with lots of appropriate cinematic yet mundane equipment, then adding one dot in each Mega-Attribute and sprinkling in some low-key Mega-Edges goes a long way towards modeling his demonstrated abilities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T05:18:45-07:00","id":1418502,"title":"","content":"Single form transformations are best handled using the dormancy edge at a rating of 4 or 5 since they will look completely different. Other options include using negative tags on the transformation to restrict it heavily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T12:41:46-07:00","id":1418570,"title":"","content":"Dormancy only works if one of the two forms has no powers whatsoever, and it doesn't by default cover the super form having lower attributes than the base form. Using the Hulk comics as an example, Bruce Banner has been shown to be an inventive genius capable of making literal super science devices, presumably due to low/moderate levels of Mega-Intellect.<br /> <br /> If I had to rework Transformation, I'd have it grant a single alternate form by default, possibly with a Tag for additional forms, although it wouldn't be a simple 1-for-1 progression. Maybe the 1st Tag grants one more form (2 total), the 2nd two more (4 total), the 3rd three more (7 total), and a 4th grants unlimited alternate forms. This models how having multiple forms is more useful, but there are severe diminishing returns since you can only gain the benefit of one set of powers at a time, so getting a growing number of additional forms at each level makes up for that. Or maybe the revised Power Suite rules would be a better fit, and a Tag like that will be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> At the first level of Transformation, I'd allow the player to strip as many dots from their character sheet as they want and use the freed up xp to buy up new traits for the alternate form. Each additional level would grant bonus xp usable only to improve the character's alternate form(s). Given that characters spend 12 xp per level of a power, the bonus xp would have to be 15+ to make up for the fact that it is only usable in their alternate form(s).<br /> <br /> I'd also expand the range of traits that can be purchased with the power to include physical Mega-Edges, as well as Mega-Cunning, since the kickstarter manuscript claims you can use Transformation to purchase sensory Mega-Edges, and would require you to first buy Mega-Cunning to meet those prerequisites, but doesn't give you the option to buy Mega-Cunning as part of the transformation. If you don't have Mega-Cunning all the time, you can't grant super senses to your shapeshifting Werewolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 10-16-2020, 03:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-16T21:21:30-07:00","id":1418635,"title":"","content":"Simply being a nova will let design stuff that is beyond normal science. Bruce Banner isn't exactly Reed Richards or Tony Stark when it comes to making gadgets, but he could also still benefit from a Superior Trait on his Intellect. The fact that he is a nova gives him access to super science dormed or not. Also Hulk isn't really dumb but he is dominated by his rage most of the time. A bad Transformation if I ever saw one. He could also have Hyde Syndrome which is similar to the way the Hulk is written. Different writes had different takes on the Hulk so you do it a number of ways.<br /> <br /> As I said I think you can achieve what you are looking for by applying negative tags to the Transformation power. The negative tag is very subjective as there ae no hard and fast rules on them, but you could use them to restrict your transformation to a single form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1580,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","user":"andrewm9","date":". 10-17-2020, 12:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1580-andrewm9","name":"andrewm9","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"69"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-19T16:03:21-07:00","id":1419095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1418570#post1418570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If I had to rework Transformation, I'd have it grant a single alternate form by default, possibly with a Tag for additional forms, although it wouldn't be a simple 1-for-1 progression. Maybe the 1st Tag grants one more form (2 total), the 2nd two more (4 total), the 3rd three more (7 total), and a 4th grants unlimited alternate forms. This models how having multiple forms is more useful, but there are severe diminishing returns since you can only gain the benefit of one set of powers at a time, so getting a growing number of additional forms at each level makes up for that. Or maybe the revised Power Suite rules would be a better fit, and a Tag like that will be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> At the first level of Transformation, I'd allow the player to strip as many dots from their character sheet as they want and use the freed up xp to buy up new traits for the alternate form. Each additional level would grant bonus xp usable only to improve the character's alternate form(s). Given that characters spend 12 xp per level of a power, the bonus xp would have to be 15+ to make up for the fact that it is only usable in their alternate form(s).<br /> <br /> I'd also expand the range of traits that can be purchased with the power to include physical Mega-Edges, as well as Mega-Cunning, since the kickstarter manuscript claims you can use Transformation to purchase sensory Mega-Edges, and would require you to first buy Mega-Cunning to meet those prerequisites, but doesn't give you the option to buy Mega-Cunning as part of the transformation. If you don't have Mega-Cunning all the time, you can't grant super senses to your shapeshifting Werewolf. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar25506_1.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"25506\" data-vbnamecard=\"25506\">Shepherdboi</a> That's similar to how mechanics in some other systems of the supers genre, with some systems handling the concept more eloquently (and with a watchfulness towards abuse) than others. Again, I don't have the kickstarter rules to even begin to be able to analyze and comment, but if that is currently not allowable, your suggestion approaches things in a manner my group and I are experienced with from other systems.<br /> <br /> Your point about being able to buy Edges dependent upon Mega-stats is a particularly spot on issue we'd have. The example of a werewolf being a very good one, since the &quot;empowered&quot; form is thematically supposed to have the ability that the baseline form specifically does <i>not</i> possess. I understand how the initial design of Edges is connected to Megas, but this does create a issue. Again, speaking without actual knowledge of the rules, if say, this is a base RAW that in order to have a Edge, you <i>must</i> have the Mega, and in regards to transformation based characters, I'd wind up house ruling that the baseline form would not require the Mega stat, but the transformed form would have to have it if its a prereq. Granted, there may be very good reasons why my solution opens a pandora's box of potential problems/abuses, but without the book before me, it seems like a logical and sensible approach.<br /> <br /> So these tags it seems have a pretty significant function beyond just acting as labeling silos. Guess I'll have to just wait for the rules before I go off into speculative wildernesses. Hopefully when they come out, some of the folks here who are savvy with the system can give us some iconic character write ups for the rest of us to use as inspired examples. Personally I've been using Herosystem and Mutants&amp;Masterminds for a very long time, and I have had many sit downs with people (or posts on forums) who are new to those systems having lots of AHA! moments from showing them how to use the various design tools in the system to better effect. A good bit of it is just learning how to translate general ideas/concepts within the system and then refining it further using the many modifiers, often in ways that aren't immediately obvious just by reading the rules.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T03:09:09-08:00","id":1426671,"title":"","content":"Just rewatched the mcu movies to get ideas for my upcoming game. Some thoughts on the avengers as trinity characters.<br /> <br /> Captain america: superior<br /> Black panther: superior with advanced tech<br /> <br /> Tony stark: mental talent<br /> Black widow: talent<br /> Hawkeye: talent<br /> <br /> Thor: 2 gen nova<br /> Hulk: nova<br /> Captain marvel: nova<br /> Scarlet witch: nova<br /> <br /> Infiniti stones: quantum artifacts<br /> <br /> Dr. Strange: Talent , using specialized gifts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T03:42:52-08:00","id":1426677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426671#post1426671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just rewatched the mcu movies to get ideas for my upcoming game. Some thoughts on the avengers as trinity characters.<br /> <br /> Captain america: superior<br /> Black panther: superior with advanced tech<br /> <br /> Tony stark: mental talent<br /> Black widow: talent<br /> Hawkeye: talent<br /> <br /> Thor: 2 gen nova<br /> Hulk: nova<br /> Captain marvel: nova<br /> Scarlet witch: nova<br /> <br /> Infiniti stones: quantum artifacts<br /> <br /> Dr. Strange: Talent , using specialized gifts</div> </div> </div> </div>So are you thinking like a whole group of novas who intermarry and shape their powers around the myth of the Asgardian gods?<br /> <br /> Also couldn\u2019t Tony Stark be a Mega-Int nova?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T03:58:10-08:00","id":1426678,"title":"","content":"Tony as a Mega-Intelligence Stealth Nova is what the developers had in mind while writing the Super-science rules.<br /> <br /> (From Endgame: \u201csince when do you know Quantum Mechanics?\u201d \u201csince last night.\u201d)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-30-2020, 07:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T14:27:07-08:00","id":1426743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426678#post1426678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tony as a Mega-Intelligence Stealth Nova is what the developers had in mind while writing the Super-science rules.<br /> <br /> (From Endgame: \u201csince when do you know Quantum Mechanics?\u201d \u201csince last night.\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T19:26:49-08:00","id":1426783,"title":"","content":"Of note, there is the new power Density with a tag that gives you your Colossus type transformation. <br /> <br /> There is also Boost which adds some dynacism, but there isn't a RAW way for Boost to give you associated Mega Edges, which seems easy enough to modify towards.<br /> <br /> You could do a Power Suite of the two, but that still doesn't account for the RAGE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T19:41:34-08:00","id":1426786,"title":"","content":"The idea for Colossus is to build the Metalic form and turn it of with Dormancy. That way you have access to everything, but the human form have no power at all, what I think is not the best solution.<br /> <br /> Same for Boost, you can boost your attributes but not mega edges, so you can\u2019t boost your durability for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T22:30:34-08:00","id":1426797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426671#post1426671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just rewatched the mcu movies to get ideas for my upcoming game. Some thoughts on the avengers as trinity characters.<br /> <br /> Captain america: superior<br /> Black panther: superior with advanced tech<br /> <br /> Tony stark: mental talent<br /> Black widow: talent<br /> Hawkeye: talent<br /> <br /> Thor: 2 gen nova<br /> Hulk: nova<br /> Captain marvel: nova<br /> Scarlet witch: nova<br /> <br /> Infiniti stones: quantum artifacts<br /> <br /> Dr. Strange: Talent , using specialized gifts</div> </div> </div> </div>If we ever get rules for the Mercer tier paramorphs, it is possible that Strange could fit their, but he definitely isn\u2019t a Talent as we know them, with their whole shtick being \u201cbadass normals\u201d whose reality editing plays out as incredible skill and luck. As magic that can be learned does not exist in the Trinity Continuum, you\u2019d have to play it loose with Strange, make him either a Psiad or a Nova to get his range of powers.<br /> <br /> First Avenger and Avengers Cap would probably be a Superior yes. But once you get to the Russo movies though he\u2019s clearly working at full Mega-Attribute level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-11-30T22:45:54-08:00","id":1426798,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426678#post1426678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tony as a Mega-Intelligence Stealth Nova is what the developers had in mind while writing the Super-science rules.<br /> <br /> (From Endgame: \u201csince when do you know Quantum Mechanics?\u201d \u201csince last night.\u201d)</div> </div> </div> </div>This. Tony goes from \u2018I built a working armor suit from scrap in a cave\u2019 (bonus: prototype micro clean energy source) to \u2018magical nanotech\u2019 in about 10 years. While designing and building just about everything else the Avengers use in that time.<br /> <br /> Edit: But not so much a \u2018stealth nova\u2019 as one who is known to be a nova but all his Quantum abilities are tied up in Mega mentals (and probably some socials) and Edges to help invent and build stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T03:32:33-08:00","id":1426810,"title":"","content":"Just a comment on this all.<br /> <br /> A guy like Kingpin is normal, except he must be 8feet tall and strong like a bull. He is not different, mutant or engineered to be like this, he just is huge.<br /> Tony Stark was a genius since he was young, basically he has the mental version of Kingpin size, far above what is considered normal, but yet normal.<br /> <br /> Yes, to build what Tony builds he need to have Mega Mental Attributes, but he\u2019s inventions are not powered by his inner power (the mini reactor is not his quantum source), and so all his inventions are essentially Nova Tech (Pepper Pots used his armor, it was not designed for her, and it was his most advanced version at the time).<br /> <br /> I would allow a Talent to invent Inspired Science to build something like a Rocketeer suit or a Hologram Projector (like the ones in Agents of Shield). Iron Man armor is completely out of the reach of a talent, but I think we miss some good stuff if we limit inventors to Novas.<br /> <br /> Concluding, Tony works much better as a Nova and his armor as Q-Tech, but there are some stuff in Marvel and DC that don\u2019t fit the Trinity paradigm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T10:29:25-08:00","id":1426835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426810#post1426810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a comment on this all.<br /> <br /> A guy like Kingpin is normal, except he must be 8feet tall and strong like a bull. He is not different, mutant or engineered to be like this, he just is huge.<br /> Tony Stark was a genius since he was young, basically he has the mental version of Kingpin size, far above what is considered normal, but yet normal.<br /> <br /> Yes, to build what Tony builds he need to have Mega Mental Attributes, but he\u2019s inventions are not powered by his inner power (the mini reactor is not his quantum source), and so all his inventions are essentially Nova Tech (Pepper Pots used his armor, it was not designed for her, and it was his most advanced version at the time).<br /> <br /> I would allow a Talent to invent Inspired Science to build something like a Rocketeer suit or a Hologram Projector (like the ones in Agents of Shield). Iron Man armor is completely out of the reach of a talent, but I think we miss some good stuff if we limit inventors to Novas.<br /> <br /> Concluding, Tony works much better as a Nova and his armor as Q-Tech, but there are some stuff in Marvel and DC that don\u2019t fit the Trinity paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem you're getting at here are one universe's conventions around the source of abilities vs another universe's. I mean Superman's an alien who is powered by yellow spectrum solar energy, not a Nova drawing on Quantum either - but the fact remains that he is best mechanically represented in this different universe as a Nova. The fact that its a contrivance of the Marvel Universe that Tony is a normal human whose mental abilitiess aren't diegetically Superhuman doesn't change the fact that they are FAR beyond anything a baseline human or even Talent is capable of. The contrivances of the ORIGINS of a characters abilities are never going to mesh when you are translating them between different settings that make different assumptions about such powers.<br /> <br /> We're getting here at the age old Exalted debate where people want Batman to be playable as a Heroic Mortal because that's the contrivance of his setting - but Exalted doesn't assume Heroic Mortals are capable of the superhuman level of abilities the DC Universe allows via &quot;peak human training&quot; - and inevitably Batman is best represented there as a Night Caste Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-01T10:51:11-08:00","id":1426838,"title":"","content":"I always thought it was funny how the old Marvel Super Heroes Basic Set claimed a score of 30 was the &quot;normal human limit,&quot; but High-Tech heroes like Tony Stark are allowed to start with scores of 50 (enhanced human limit) in Fighting (why?), Intuition (common sense/battle savvy), and Psyche (willpower), and a score of 75 (beyond human) in Reason (logic/comprehension). I found it stranger that Tony Stark only had Reason: 40 (enhanced human), Intuition: 20 (olympic-level), and Psyche: 6 (average human). Professor X and Forge also have a Reason score of 40, while Mister Fantastic has a Reason score of 50. None of these iconic characters hit the attribute cap on their Reason ability.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 12-01-2020, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T03:04:59-08:00","id":1426945,"title":"","content":"I think people sometimes underestimate what Inspired Super-Science is capable of. Just take a look at some of the examples in the core book: stealth armor and freeze rays both make the list. DCU's Mr. Freeze and Captain Cold could both be done 100% as Talents, just on the basis of that freeze ray example. (Well, Mr. Freeze would also need a containment suit; but I have no doubt that could also be managed through Inspired tech.) <br /> <br /> What sold me on the notion that Tony Stark is a Nova was the exchange I cited from Endgame: in <i>one night</i>, he became an expert on quantum mechanics and its application to time travel. <i>That's</i> Mega-Intelligence, and not just one or two dots of it; I wouldn't be surprised if he was in the 4 to 5 dots range.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":".  typo 12-02-2020, 11:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T13:34:46-08:00","id":1427020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426835#post1426835\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The problem you're getting at here are one universe's conventions around the source of abilities vs another universe's. I mean Superman's an alien who is powered by yellow spectrum solar energy, not a Nova drawing on Quantum either - but the fact remains that he is best mechanically represented in this different universe as a Nova. The fact that its a contrivance of the Marvel Universe that Tony is a normal human whose mental abilitiess aren't diegetically Superhuman doesn't change the fact that they are FAR beyond anything a baseline human or even Talent is capable of. The contrivances of the ORIGINS of a characters abilities are never going to mesh when you are translating them between different settings that make different assumptions about such powers.<br /> <br /> We're getting here at the age old Exalted debate where people want Batman to be playable as a Heroic Mortal because that's the contrivance of his setting - but Exalted doesn't assume Heroic Mortals are capable of the superhuman level of abilities the DC Universe allows via &quot;peak human training&quot; - and inevitably Batman is best represented there as a Night Caste Solar.</div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1098_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1098\" data-vbnamecard=\"1098\">glamourweaver</a> Good points those. With my circle one of the things that was often bandied about when discussing such things was what a character was capable of at various periods of their history, and how abilities shifted under various authors to fit their story. Comic characters are decidedly <i>not</i> consistent because they're works of fiction and pay zero attention to being formally represented in a RPG. And of course, the two franchises have different premises and themes that were heavily influenced by the Comics Code slamming down on their creative directions. <br /> <br /> Usually when things of this sort pop up in game discussions of say, &quot;I want to play Batman in Exalted&quot;, the first thing I do is suggest to them not to duplicate a character with a dozen different writers and power levels within a game system, but to sum them up in a short blurb. I.E. a individual capable of incredible feats of stealth and investigation, a skilled combatant, and a master of contingencies and exploiting weaknesses, now select abilities to grow into that. Makes it much easier for a player to assemble and portray a character inspired by a iconic character.<br /> <br /> This dovetails into another talk I recently had, what our setting would be. Marvel and DC are not the same as the Aberrant setting, the former two are exceptionally deep with history and character lore but to attempt to faithfully recreate them via Aberrant means you're introducing taint and the other assorted aspects of Aberrant's power sources, of which magic is absent. The DCU has a good deal more mysticism and magic than the MU, but both have it and Aberrant doesn't (at least not by default). <br /> <br /> So the question was which setting are we using, and then what modifications have to be made for a Aberrant game. I decided that I was going to borrow liberally from MU/DCU, and include both PSI since I have Aeon, and magic (though not touching anything from WoD/CoD to govern magic) as a power source besides quantum energies. Then selectively choose characters, but still map them to Aberrants system, so the likelihood of Superman wearing a harness to drag a moon or dive to the deepest part of the ocean and push the earth off it's axis by a few inches isn't a thing. But Batman being a Darkstar or Tony Stark having meta-intelligence and making quantum science tech is definitely within reach and in either case, I'm not concerned with faithfully recreating a character's sum history from a dozen different authors, I'm concerned with projecting my take of a iconic character within a setting of my choosing, at a level of my choosing through Aberrant's rules (mostly, until my grumpy old man syndrome kicks in and I start tweaking or performing system surgery).<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1426945#post1426945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think people sometimes underestimate what Inspired Super-Science is capable of. Just take a look at some of the examples in the core book: stealth armor and freeze rays both make the list. DCU's Mr. Freeze and Captain Cold could both be done 100% as Talents, just on the basis of that freeze ray example. (Well, Mr. Freeze would also need a containment suit; but I have no doubt that could also be managed through Inspired tech.)<br /> <br /> What sold me on the notion that Tony Stark is a Nova was the exchange I cited from Endgame: in <i>one night</i>, he became an expert on quantum mechanics and its application to time travel. <i>That's</i> Mega-Intelligence, and not just one or two dots of it; I wouldn't be surprised if he was in the 4 to 5 dots range.</div> </div> </div> </div>To paraphrase Clarke, super-science can be indistinguishable from magic. IMO the only reason we can't as readily imagine possibilities is due to limitations of our own knowledge and imagination. Not to be dismissive or disputing your suggested rating, but Stark's scene from Endgame is one of those examples of a writer taking the role of a character and giving the story's gateway solution to him as the most qualified voice, with no consideration of how that would be represented as a stat in a game. <br /> <br /> What I would find interesting to consider is given the portrayal of Stark's beliefs and feelings, having now learned that bit of esoteric science, what <i>else</i> does he do with what he learned once the dust settles on the current story?<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T13:45:52-08:00","id":1427023,"title":"","content":"I really don't think Strange is a talent. I can't think of one thing he does which involves lucky coincidences (any more than movies generally have.) Yes, he can manipulate time, WITH THE TIME GEM. Anyone can do that, though, if they know how. It's not a function of his being a talent. He's more of a nova with Elemental Mastery (magic) and a lot of dots in Technique.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:01:08-08:00","id":1427026,"title":"","content":"I think the point in Strange as Talent (tier 3 talent, at least) is that he can reach through dimensions mainly. it is just said in the movie that they use &quot;spells&quot; to siphon energy form other dimensions to alter their own reality, basically a conscious way to use flux, while the regular talent can only use it unconsciously.<br /> <br /> Yes, it can be created as a character using a Nova, the same way you can create Professor X as a Mega Social Nova or Batman as a low Quantum Nova, if it fits your game I think it's valid.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:12:48-08:00","id":1427029,"title":"","content":"Just to plug his work: it's decidedly noncanon, but Mateus Luz' <b>Tomes of Inspiration</b> (see his signature) would handle Dr. Strange quite well. If you're willing to bend the rationale a bit, it could also handle Zatanna and John Constantine as well. It's basically \u201cTalents as the basis for magic\u201d, with a healthy dose of Clarke's Law thrown in. <br /> <br /> Again, though, not canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:18:33-08:00","id":1427035,"title":"","content":"I also think equating different dimensions with alternate worlds (and therefore Talents) is incorrect from an MCU perspective. The Quantum Realm is considered a different dimension in the MCU (as shown in Dr. Strange's movie when he's knocked through a bunch of them) despite being modeled as the micro-field in Aberrant and not an alternate world. Dormamu's realm and the mirror realm are more like different states of existence as opposed to alternate worlds.<br /> <br /> Trying to point at one thing he does, travel to two different dimensions, as proof he's a talent when he does a bunch of other things which are not possible for talents is a step too far for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:27:02-08:00","id":1427038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427035#post1427035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think equating different dimensions with alternate worlds (and therefore Talents) is incorrect from an MCU perspective. The Quantum Realm is considered a different dimension in the MCU (as shown in Dr. Strange's movie when he's knocked through a bunch of them) despite being modeled as the micro-field in Aberrant and not an alternate world. Dormamu's realm and the mirror realm are more like different states of existence as opposed to alternate worlds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Parallel dimensions include realities extremely similar to ours but also realities that work on different physics laws. Sliders (the old series) and Event Horizon (Terror Sci-fi) uses this premise.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Trying to point at one thing he does, travel to two different dimensions, as proof he's a talent when he does a bunch of other things which are not possible for talents is a step too far for me. </div> </div> </div>He is not a talent, he is a magician, but magic don't exist in MCU, all we are doing is suggesting ways to simulating his powers based on his fluffy.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar421_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"421\" data-vbnamecard=\"421\">Dataweaver</a> Thanks for the reference!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:51:15-08:00","id":1427042,"title":"","content":"Talents as Magicians reminds me of The Death Gate Cycle series of novels (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Death_Gate_Cycle\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Death_Gate_Cycle</a>). The two main factions (Sartans and Patryns) are super powerful probability manipulators on a level with the Scarlet Witch, able to perceive even the most absurdly unlikely things and make them real.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to model Doctor Strange as a Talent, you could argue he started as a normal Talent, able to succeed at procedures no other neurosurgeon could duplicate, then was awakened to a much higher level of ability by the Ancient One.<br /> <br /> edit: Of course this would imply that Talents like Hawkeye and Black Widow could also be awakened as Magicians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25506,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","user":"Shepherdboi","date":". 12-02-2020, 05:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T14:53:08-08:00","id":1427043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427042#post1427042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Talents as Magicians reminds me of The Death Gate Cycle series of novels (<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Death_Gate_Cycle\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Death_Gate_Cycle</a>). The two main factions (Sartans and Patryns) are super powerful probability manipulators on a level with the Scarlet Witch, able to perceive even the most absurdly unlikely things and make them real.<br /> <br /> If you really wanted to model Doctor Strange as a Talent, you could argue he started as a normal Talent, able to succeed at procedures no other neurosurgeon could duplicate, then was awakened to a much higher level of ability by the Ancient One.</div> </div> </div> </div>First half: Great example!<br /> <br /> Second half: Indeed!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T15:24:25-08:00","id":1427045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shepherdboi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427042#post1427042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">edit: Of course this would imply that Talents like Hawkeye and Black Widow could also be awakened as Magicians.</div> </div> </div> </div> Only if there's a reliable way to do it. Assuming that \u201cAwakening\u201d a Talent to a higher Magician-like tier is even possible, the means of doing so would need to be defined; and they <i>might</i> be \u201cblind luck\u201d, ironically enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T15:43:11-08:00","id":1427049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427045#post1427045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Only if there's a reliable way to do it. Assuming that \u201cAwakening\u201d a Talent to a higher Magician-like tier is even possible, the means of doing so would need to be defined; and they <i>might</i> be \u201cblind luck\u201d, ironically enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the Doctor Strange movie, the Ancient One apparently did it by punching his astral body right out of his flesh. In the comics, he studied with the Ancient One, then had magic powers. Either way, if Doctor Strange was a normal Talent who became a magical Super-Talent, it was probably because of something another Super-Talent did to him.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T15:59:11-08:00","id":1427052,"title":"","content":"Probably. But it's also possible that she was only able to do it because he had a special affinity for magic that he wasn't previously aware of, something that most Talents don't have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T18:54:32-08:00","id":1427080,"title":"","content":"I think Hawkeye and Black Widow were capable of learning magic if they dedicated enough to do so in Marvel universe. There are many magicians, including the guy that lost his movements, that were not THAT special before and become good enough.<br /> <br /> Strange had the knowledge of science and medicine that would help to understand a few things, he also speak a few languages and had eidetic memory, all that together gave him some advantage, and the desire to recover his hands made him specially dedicated. His objective with the Eye of Agamoto was to reverse the damage in his hands, and it end up in the plot we had in the movie.<br /> <br /> That is the thing with magic in many settings, anyone can learn, some people have advantages, but anyone dedicated enough could do that. Harry Potter setting requires a genetic predisposition, for example, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s needed in Marvel universe. So, maybe practicing the mystical arts with masters of magic expose your body to flux and turn you into a Talent or even a Excelsior (Super Talent).<br /> <br /> Edit: Removed DC from last paragraph as it\u2019s not the case for DC (thanks Dataweaver)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-02-2020, 10:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T19:04:17-08:00","id":1427084,"title":"","content":"I don't know about Marvel; but in DC, Zatanna is <i>homo magus</i> and can wield magic because it's in her blood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T19:36:39-08:00","id":1427088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427080#post1427080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Hawkeye and Black Widow were capable of learning magic if they dedicated enough to do so in Marvel universe. There are many magicians, including the guy that lost his movements, that were not THAT special before and become good enough.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I want there to be story in which Barton turns over the Hawkeye identity to Kate Bishop, learns magic and creates spectral arrows (or some kind of cantrips not necessarily archery-related).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-02T20:42:34-08:00","id":1427095,"title":"","content":"My whole post was about me juicing for a aeon campaign and watching the mcu for inspiration. My players are green to trinity, so being able to give them a reference was the goal. <br /> That said..<br /> <br /> Captain america doesn't show any nova qualities that a superior can't do with momentum.<br /> <br /> Strange consciously uses flux because he is aware of it.<br /> <br /> Still open to starks splat. Money a smarts can go along way. Plus he took/copied wakanda tech for infinity war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T05:08:33-08:00","id":1427127,"title":"","content":"If you're trying to give them references for Talents, Black Widow and Hawkeye are much better examples of Talents as they're presented in the core book. Strange does things even Mercer hasn't been referenced doing.<br /> <br /> Iron Man is a Nova with Mega-Intelligence and uses a power suit full of q-tech. His arc reactor is a great example of q-tech which becomes nova tech (and then eventually core tech) over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T13:44:06-08:00","id":1427197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427095#post1427095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My whole post was about me juicing for a aeon campaign and watching the mcu for inspiration. My players are green to trinity, so being able to give them a reference was the goal.<br /> That said..<br /> <br /> Captain america doesn't show any nova qualities that a superior can't do with momentum.<br /> <br /> Strange consciously uses flux because he is aware of it.<br /> <br /> Still open to starks splat. Money a smarts can go along way. Plus he took/copied wakanda tech for infinity war.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Another inspiration series from the MCU are the X-Men, though there are a number of differing powers that don't represent psi powers, Professor X and Jean Grey, even Psylocke, are all Psi. <br /> <br /> Minor tidbit: at one time there was a series of books released by Marvel Studios that were a paper &quot;wiki&quot; wherein each character within the MCU was written up with history, status and powers. Most of the X-Men had powers that, though a result of the extra gene in their DNA, had some application of psi. For instance, Colossus was said to possess the &quot;psionic ability&quot; to transform his organic carbon molecules with organic metal, resulting in vastly increasing his strength, resilience, etc. Cyclops had the &quot;psionic ability&quot; to open a portal to a dimension of pure energy through his eyes.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I'm not defending the essays at the time, my friends and I eye rolled over plenty of those power descriptions and joked how the writers used the word &quot;psionic&quot; instead of &quot;magic&quot; to sound more educated while being too lazy to think of any other way to describe how the powers worked. <br /> <br /> RE: Captain America<br /> <br /> Less certain about being just a superior. Though as mentioned before, it depends on the writer and what they give him as abilities. One series I read he was able to go with paratroopers without a chute, if he suffered any injuries from the jump, he would heal up in a matter of minutes. That same writer gave him a much greater physical density, which made him more resistant to harm as if he were wearing a full suit of body armor as well as much stronger, able to flip a car onto it's side with minimal effort or slam into a tank with his shield and rattle the crew inside silly. That same regenerative capability made him highly resistant to toxins, and diseases, including fatigue poisons and what not. Many of those abilities could be represented by a Darkstar Nova.<br /> <br /> But again, repeating myself, depends on the writer. I'm not expressly disagreeing with you so much as pointing out that it depends on which stories one is referencing to represent him.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T16:56:45-08:00","id":1427220,"title":"","content":"Perhaps we could make MCU and DC villains and monsters using the Aeon Trinity Era Aberrant rules. They could be picked from less known or lower tier antagonists, or mostly forgotten main-line villains. That would serve as good inspiration for Aberrants, Mutants and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u201cHumpty had always sat on walls, it was his way.\u201d </span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">\u2015 </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:Lato\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Jasper Fforde, </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#181818\"><span style=\"font-family:Merriweather\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://www.goodreads.com/work/quotes/2504943\" target=\"_blank\">The Big Over Easy</a></span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1756-mythadvocate","name":"MythAdvocate","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1756_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T17:46:55-08:00","id":1427230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427197#post1427197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> RE: Captain America<br /> <br /> Less certain about being just a superior. Though as mentioned before, it depends on the writer and what they give him as abilities. One series I read he was able to go with paratroopers without a chute, if he suffered any injuries from the jump, he would heal up in a matter of minutes. That same writer gave him a much greater physical density, which made him more resistant to harm as if he were wearing a full suit of body armor as well as much stronger, able to flip a car onto it's side with minimal effort or slam into a tank with his shield and rattle the crew inside silly. That same regenerative capability made him highly resistant to toxins, and diseases, including fatigue poisons and what not. Many of those abilities could be represented by a Darkstar Nova.<br /> <br /> But again, repeating myself, depends on the writer. I'm not expressly disagreeing with you so much as pointing out that it depends on which stories one is referencing to represent him.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like Ultimate Cap. He was one of the most dangerous characters in that universe. If we're using a template from the quick rules, would you think superstar Cap is a melee range fighter or a Tank?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T18:11:14-08:00","id":1427235,"title":"","content":"Ultimate Cap was a great character, and his powers were pretty much consistent, definitely not \u201ctop human physique\u201d, but superhuman. But he can be described as a Superior with not much difficulty. You can build most of the X-Men using only superior powers.<br /> <br /> Ultimate Cap has at least the following powers:<br /> Balancing Act 1, Hardened 3, Might Leap 1, Power Lifter 2, Speedster 1, Superior Recover 4 (maybe 5), Lightning Reflexes 3 and Tactician 2 (maybe 3).<br /> <br /> Not a brand new superior, but, Captain America, he has be fighting Nazis and Commies since 1941!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-03-2020, 09:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T18:15:41-08:00","id":1427236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MythAdvocate</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427220#post1427220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps we could make MCU and DC villains and monsters using the Aeon Trinity Era Aberrant rules. They could be picked from less known or lower tier antagonists, or mostly forgotten main-line villains. That would serve as good inspiration for Aberrants, Mutants and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am still to test it, but the rules for Aberrants in Aeon probably build better adversaries for Novas than the rules for antagonist Novas in Aberrant. AND it\u2019s far less work to build to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T19:48:14-08:00","id":1427242,"title":"","content":"On a defensive note about strange, in his movie it is explained that they use artifacts to enhance or support their powers. Now how or who created these artifacts is left up to writers of script, comic, or campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-03T22:10:01-08:00","id":1427246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cKnight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1427242#post1427242\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On a defensive note about strange, in his movie it is explained that they use artifacts to enhance or support their powers. Now how or who created these artifacts is left up to writers of script, comic, or campaign.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is kind of explained in the movie that they were created as some magic Is too powerful to be cast all the time, and it\u2019s better to use from the artifacts. It implies that any one of the masters of mystical arts could create magical items if dedicated time for that, what probably just a few do. But the portal ring is pretty common among them, so probably many of them produce or one guy produces lots of them.<br /> <br /> Not Cannon, but the entire idea of this post is a bit anti-cannon, so... check the 2nd and 3rd lines in my signature. You could build them and give the feeling that differentiates Iron-Man armor from Doctor Strange artifacts. Fists of Flux was on sale for Black Friday and Cyber Monday, maybe still is, Tomes of Inspiration is PWYW.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-04T19:18:29-08:00","id":1427321,"title":"","content":"I've got them . Tomes of inspiration actually is the reason I feel strange was a strong talent. Granted he had access to powerful artifacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2421-cknight","name":"cKnight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"47"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T14:56:33-08:00","id":1429071,"title":"","content":"Pardon my ramble on this but, I'm currently frustrated and very annoyed with the books. I'll spare y'all a rant on the subject, other than to say it's damn annoying when what you're looking for is in a text box that seems like it was slapped in semi-randomly as an afterthought with no references in the index. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway.<br /> <br /> My question is there's a term that's getting bandied about within the TC threads that I haven't been able to track down. So if one of y'all could set me straight on this and where I can find it, I'd be grateful. WTF do I find info about &quot;Superiors&quot;??? There's no mention of them in the TC core book, which if they're a thing and since the TC Core is like...core, figured they'd at least be mentioned in the lexicon to give me an idea of where I might find out more about them to at least know what they are thematically. Unfortunately, that's not the case, so...yeah...if someone could kindly fill me in?<br /> <br /> On a related note specific to this thread: <br /> I finally had some free time this week to go through an exercise of creating a few Novas and I reached a (disappointing) conclusion that I've seen mentioned on the board by others but didn't quite get till I ran into a bunch of ceilings and walls designing Novas. To be fair, I walked into the Aberrant book with expectations of Storypath doing basically, Superheroes. However, much to my disappointment that's a mistaken assumption. It's not a &quot;Supers&quot; game system, it's a <i>specific take </i>on the Supers genre. Aberrant is part of a franchise and meta-story, thus Novas follow conceptual limitations and adhere to a limited thematic track to keep them in line with the meta-story of the product line where one day, they're the inhuman antagonists.<br /> <br /> Basically since having started this thread I've come to see that one can at best use MU/DCU characters for <i>inspiration</i> and recreating them (even conservatively) involves compromises that leave one saying the character is a &lt;name&gt;-ish build (i.e. Batman-ish, Green Lantern-ish, Wolverine-ish). Even certain arch types typical of a Supers game aren't the same in Aberrant game as presented in other rule sets, beyond broad brush strokes. <br /> <br /> That said, I'm still a fan of Storypath's system and believe it <i>can</i> do a Supers game, but Aberrant as is does not serve up the same offerings as say Mutants &amp; Masterminds, it will take a good bit of work on my part to create a set of custom rules on my end to recreate a &quot;classic Supers&quot; setting via Storypath's systems. Given my time limitations, I'm likely going to have to hope some creative, like-minded soul will beat me to it and publish it on the Vault.<br /> <br /> Finally: If some of you would like to post representations of characters from the MU/DCU here still, know that you'll have at least one avid reader appreciative of your attempt. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T15:33:54-08:00","id":1429080,"title":"","content":"Superiors are \u201ccontrolled eruption Novas\u201d that Nihon created sometime late 2040s. They are referenced in Aeon and fully stated in Aexpansion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288643/Trinity-Continuum-Aeon-Aexpansion?cPath=8329_22321\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ath=8329_22321</a><br /> <br /> Now, on building any character faithfully to their nature, it\u2019s a bit out of the scope of Aberrant. The powers presented allow you to build most of the characters with some effort, it it will be really hard to make them feel the same because the setting is different from the begging, Quantum Power is not mutation, quantum power is not magic, it\u2019s not the powers that you gain from being inter the yellow sun, or whatever. Same for Transcendence, the concept was created to fit the setting and the setting only, where the supers will evolve (what is very unusual in comics) and become unstable (what is not that unusual in comics, to be fair).<br /> <br /> The entire nature of magic not existing in TC, that Psi and Quantum are opposing forces, and other details are strongly connected to Aberrant system and setting. YET, nothing impedes you of building characters using Aberrant system and a few tweaks to make it closer to the original idea. I am certain that more than a few writers will bring some good stuff to the Nexus with some options to make Aberrant more \u201cgeneric Suppers friendly\u201d, I will for sure!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 12-19-2020, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T16:52:43-08:00","id":1429087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1429080#post1429080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Superiors are \u201ccontrolled eruption Novas\u201d that Nihon created sometime late 2040s. They are referenced in Aeon and fully stated in Aexpansion.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/288643/Trinity-Continuum-Aeon-Aexpansion?cPath=8329_22321\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...ath=8329_22321</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24985_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24985\" data-vbnamecard=\"24985\">Mateus Luz</a> Ahhh, ok. Thanks for the guidance. That explains the gap, I haven't picked up Aexpansion yet and Aeon is still awaiting a deeper dive. I have come to the same conclusion regarding Quantum and other factors as you mentioned, and I agree, I have to roll up my sleeves for house rules to address stepping outside the box that Aberrant takes place in. Like I said, it's a bit disappointing, but understanding that now having worked my way through the creation rules I find myself less frustrated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Reality is a matter of perception, challenging one's own or that of others is not a crime, it is a service.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12415-seeker1728","name":"Seeker1728","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-19T21:17:53-08:00","id":1429114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Seeker1728</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1429071#post1429071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, I'm still a fan of Storypath's system and believe it <i>can</i> do a Supers game, but Aberrant as is does not serve up the same offerings as say Mutants &amp; Masterminds, it will take a good bit of work on my part to create a set of custom rules on my end to recreate a &quot;classic Supers&quot; setting via Storypath's systems. Given my time limitations, I'm likely going to have to hope some creative, like-minded soul will beat me to it and publish it on the Vault.<br /> <br /> Finally: If some of you would like to post representations of characters from the MU/DCU here still, know that you'll have at least one avid reader appreciative of your attempt.</div> </div> </div> </div>If going for a classic comic book feel, I'd play up similarities between Transformations/Transcendence and the soap opera-ish nature of comics. Namorita's skin once turned blue, while the Wasp briefly had an insect-like appearance. Ant-Man and the Scarlet Witch have had recurring mental issues. Spider-Man had six arms for awhile, and Wolverine's appearance became more primitive after the adamantium was ripped from his body. All of these could be explained as persistent low-level and mid-level transformations, which were later bought off using some house rules.<br /> <br /> If someone buys Nova traits with a Transformation/Transcendence discount, you could let the Aberrant traits go into remission by paying the xp difference later in the campaign. If they gain a Transformation via too much Transcendence, just make it temporary, lasting at least as many story arcs as the character's Transcendence level, then allow them to shed it after a suitably epic character development.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25506-shepherdboi","name":"Shepherdboi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25506_1.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T15:46:27-08:00","id":1429253,"title":"","content":"As someone who has played just about every major superhero game out there, I have to say that any game will drop the ball on some level (sometimes a lot of levels) when it comes to making comic book heroes in it. And when using a game like Aberrant who is not designed to be a generic superhero system? I would recommend just going for the feel of things and not an exact one-for-one replication. Comics are inconsistent and writers will expand on things or change things up. <br /> <br /> Also, if you want to do Strange, make him a Psiad. His powers are not Psionic in nature but a Psiad has the same level of power that Strange shows in the movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-20T20:13:36-08:00","id":1429286,"title":"","content":"Both Dr. Strange and Dr. Fate pull power in from beyond this reality. Frankly both of them along with Zatanna, the White Witch of Naltor, and Scarlett Witch, all are better modelled using Mage spheres. Just decide how much they cost in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Johnny Thunder has a Quantum Construct that has Mage Spheres and a personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 12-20-2020, 11:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T01:07:04-08:00","id":1429308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Astromancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1429286#post1429286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Both Dr. Strange and Dr. Fate pull power in from beyond this reality. Frankly both of them along with Zatanna, the White Witch of Naltor, and Scarlett Witch, all are better modelled using Mage spheres. Just decide how much they cost in Aberrant.<br /> <br /> Johnny Thunder has a Quantum Construct that has Mage Spheres and a personality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hmmmm...someone who uses the Order of Hermes suggest to use Mage Spheres. Go figure....<br /> <br /> lol...j/k.<br /> <br /> In all seriousness,I said to use Psiads to emulate Strange because the array of powers available are great (possibly greater array than a Mage if you use similar XP amounts) and also a Psiad can bond to &quot;magic items&quot; similar to biotech.<br /> <br /> I am not saying that Strange's powers do not come from another dimension nor am I saying that a Psiad's does. I am saying to use a Psiad to be the way to model a mage like Strange from a mechanical point of view and not a thematic model.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/786-thedonnie","name":"thedonnie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T04:22:08-08:00","id":1429329,"title":"","content":"Indeed. The eventual \u00c6gis era will be leaving heavily into that notion, too: it has been stated that one of the inspirations for it was a line in the original Adventure! book that compared daredevils, mesmerists, and stalwarts to fantasy heroes, magicians, and gods, respectively. <br /> <br /> But that brings up another possibility: rather than using Psion Aptitudes or Mage Spheres to represent the likes of Doctor Fate or Doctor Strange, you might go with Scion Purviews.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T09:18:27-08:00","id":1429371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1417071-dcu-mu-character-builds-for-aberrant?p=1429329#post1429329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But that brings up another possibility: rather than using Psion Aptitudes or Mage Spheres to represent the likes of Doctor Fate or Doctor Strange, you might go with Scion Purviews.</div> </div> </div> </div>Scion Purviews are both rules lighter and already part of the Storypath system, so it\u2019s much easier to adapt, and you get pretty much all the feeling of comics spellcasters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-21T13:57:12-08:00","id":1429414,"title":"","content":"Aha! I knew there had been a thread like this after the KS doc dropped-<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350041-superhero-conversions\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350041-superhero-conversions\"> Superhero Conversions - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350041-superhero-conversions\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1350041-superhero-conversions </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> In an effort to keep myself fresh with the System, indulge my inner geek, and create new Paths, I am working on a number of conversions of pre-existing heroes to </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}